## THE AUTHOR'S WRITING

Below are real passages from the author. Note the RANGE — some are long and formal, others are short and rough. Some use many connectors, others use none. This variation is part of the voice.

### Formal academic passages (long sentences, connectors, citations)

"Public libraries being hub of information have a very vital role to play as public libraries are established to provide timely information resources, which communicate experience and ideas from one person to another and make them easily and freely available to all people, regardless of race, nationality, age, gender, religion, language, disability, employment status and educational attainment."

"The improved socio-economic and political status of an individual or the community obviously depends largely upon knowledge and information, hence reading is one of the most important means for the acquisition of knowledge and information."

"Information and its effective, proper dissemination and utilization are an integral and very powerful force to reckon with in socio-economic and political development."

"Socio-economic and political development especially in developing countries is becoming knowledge and information based; therefore, knowledge will inevitably serve as the driving force to enhance productivity, economic growth and performance."

"To this end, therefore, public libraries are the only 'free' agencies that provide a variety of reading services for every individual no matter his status, educational background and age."

"Public libraries are therefore the main arena through which the overall information resources in various areas of knowledge are made freely available to all members of the community irrespective of age, sex, religion, cultural background, educational standard as well as political and social inclination."

"According to Rontos (2013) he argued that overall development is also associated with the degree of human development that is by the level of health, the degree of access to knowledge and the level of well-being prevailing in a given country, as a wider notion than economic development."

"Development practitioners are increasingly aware of the role of social and political factors in shaping development outcomes as contained in World Bank (2005), which asserts that political power relations tend to reflect and shape social and economic distribution patterns in so-called 'inequality traps' that constrain economic growth and poverty reduction and increase social tensions."

### Shorter, rougher passages (less formal, more direct)

"Education solely depends on the availability of the right information at the right time."

"It involves the development of the whole person intellectually, psychologically, socially, vocationally, religiously or morally. This is the reason why information is seen as an integral part of national development."

"Both public libraries have a sizable collection of books, magazines, journals and newspaper and they are also connected to internet."

"The role of public libraries cannot be overemphasized especially in developing countries. Public libraries are seen as agencies for continuing education both for the young, old and physically challenged members of the community."

"government effectiveness, significant reduction of income and wealth inequalities, large social transformations, reduced corruption and democratic political system. For this to be achieved successfully the society must be well informed and knowledgeable about their basic rights and responsibilities."

### Descriptive passages (specific names, places, numbers)

"Government District Public Library Bundi is princely a library situated in Biggest Government School Campus with Huge Building and right now curetted by Mr. Joginder Singh. It is established in 1956 and having Collection of about 47067 Books."

"Govt. Panchayat Samiti Public Library Kaithoon is in Kota District and established in year 2001 and now it is running in its own building made in year 2006 by the Co-operation of Raja Ram Mohun Roy Library Foundation (RRRLF) Kolkata."

"Right Now there is a total 278 Public Libraries in Rajasthan whereas 50 are fully under the control of Department and rests are run under school premises partially by School Librarian."

### Data reporting passages (formulaic, repetitive)

"From table 4 above, the study shows that 58% of the registered users, 55% none registered users and 67% of freely abled users of the public libraries use the libraries for getting information while15% of registered users, 18% of none registered users get information from outside the library. Further more, 27% of registered users as well as none registered users use the internet to get information."

"In table 8 above, about 82% of registered users, 86% of non registered users and 67% of freely abled users are of the view that their level of awareness has increase by visiting public libraries while only 18% of registered users, 14% of non registered users and 33% of freely abled users are of the view that there was no increase in the level of their awareness."

"Furthermore, 12% of registered users and 9% of none registered users are not satisfy with the information resources."

